# 18. Final MVP Acceptance Scenario

The final MVP must allow a beginner to complete the following activity without external instruction.

1. Open NetVerse.
2. Create VPC `10.0.0.0/16`.
3. Add Availability Zones A and B.
4. Add public subnet `10.0.1.0/24`.
5. Add private subnet `10.0.2.0/24`.
6. Place EC2 instances in both subnets.
7. Understand their private IP allocations.
8. Send traffic between instances and observe local VPC routing.
9. Create an internet gateway.
10. Configure a public route table.
11. Assign a public IPv4 address to the public EC2.
12. Test outbound internet access.
13. Create a NAT gateway with an Elastic IP.
14. Configure the private default route.
15. Test private EC2 outbound internet connectivity.
16. Modify security group rules to block traffic.
17. Observe which packet is dropped and why.
18. Fix the rules.
19. Replay successful packet communication.
20. Save the completed network topology.

The interface must visually demonstrate the effect of each action.

**This is the definition of a completed NetVerse MVP.**

